 "notes": "Kinds kept: all 5 planned (Arrack renamed from 'Arrack & palm spirit'). Rum style traditions (Jamaican, Demerara, Barbados, Cuban/Spanish) are types, not kinds. Clairin placed as an archetype under Rhum agricole (cane-juice spirit; old Clairin Sajous model kept as its version). Chamarel models kept in m. Old cachaça models without makers given their brand name as maker (Yaguara, Novo Fogo, Leblon, Pitú, Velho Barreiro, Sagatiba, Santo Grau, Cachaça 61). Left out: Planteray versions (no retrieved page listed expressions; drinksint fetch returned empty); Rhum Clément expressions (page lists none); Diplomático founding year (sources only say late 1950s); Sailor Jerry launch year (not found). Wikipedia El Dorado_rum, Diplomático and Sailor Jerry articles 404. Rhum Clément page mentions no founder. Charanda (Mexico) and other world cane spirits not added."
